Keep `.a` files out of the unified dependency directory of the Windows process wrapper.

On Windows, `process_wrapper` merges every `-Ldependency=` directory into one, to keep the command line short. It
scans each directory with `read_dir`, so it also sees files that are no input of the action. `rules_rust` puts a
`lib<name>.a` symlink next to each rlib, for `cc_common.link`. With `experimental_use_cc_common_link`, Bazel builds
those symlinks while sibling `Rustc` actions scan the directory, and the copy fails with "Access is denied".

`-L dependency=` only searches for crates, and no crate is a `.a` file, so skip the extension.
